  "term": "experiential psychotherapy",
  "definition": "Experiential psychotherapy is a form of therapy that emphasizes direct experience and action in session rather than talking alone. In the source material, it involves guided role-play to help people explore feelings, gain insight, and work on personal and relationship problems and possible solutions.",
